  "title": "Recover before closing uncertain posts; fixed codes on transport errors; test the recovery selector",
  "detail": "Thank you: the spec's test-3 attack passes. A marker embedded in A doesn't acknowledge [B], exactly one genuine [B] post follows, and the substring and author mutations are caught. Source is 196 lines against the 250 stop. Three reproduced findings remain.\n\n1. **Recovery before closure (requirement 4).** `src/integrations/issue-lifecycle.ts:365` re-checks the stored body's privacy before attempting marker recovery, and a failed check marks the effect `done`. If GitHub accepted the POST, the response was lost, and the private-string inspection is unavailable after a reopen, recovery makes zero comment GETs and closes the checkpoint with `commentId: null`, even though the comment exists. Recover first, using the independently generated envelope and the checkpointed posting identity. Apply the outgoing-body checks only before a new POST, and when inspection is unavailable, make no new POST.\n\n2. **Fixed diagnostics on transport errors (requirement 2).** `issue-lifecycle.ts:442` passes the exception to `logFailure` (line 64), which logs `String(error)`. `redactCredentials` doesn't remove configured private strings, so a `gh` transport error that echoes the body leaks a private string into the logs. Log a fixed failure code (and the HTTP status if it's numeric) and never the exception text, on this path and on every other publication failure path in the lifecycle.\n\n3. **The recovery selector needs a test.** The recovery-pause test switches the run back to `waiting_input` before reopening (`test/issue-queue.test.ts:1905`), so active-run selection hides the new `recovering` selector. Removing `recovering` from `src/db/store.ts:1427` still passes all 90 Q4 tests. Add: a cancelled run with settled labels, recovery paused at page 2, then reopen. It must fail with that selector removed.\n\nThe review's regression cases follow. Adopt them (adjusting to the fixture as needed). Each must fail before the fix and pass after:\n\n```ts\ntest(\"REVIEW: uncertain accepted question recovers even when inspection becomes unavailable\", async () => {\n  const f = await lifecycleFixture();\n  const q = f.store.askQuestion(f.run.id, \"safe question\");\n  f.store.updateRun(f.run.id, { status: \"waiting_input\" });\n  f.h.afterWrite = (args) => {\n    if (args[1]?.endsWith(\"/comments\")) throw new Error(\"lost response\");\n  };\n  await f.poll();\n  expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"pending\", page: 1 });\n  expect(f.h.comments.get(7)).toHaveLength(1);\n  f.reopen();\n  f.h.afterWrite = undefined;\n  mkdirSync(join(f.h.cfg.paths.configDir, \"private-strings.txt\"));\n  f.h.calls.length = 0;\n  await f.poll();\n  expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"done\", commentId: 7001 });\n  expect(f.h.calls.some(a => a[1]?.includes(\"/comments?\"))).toBe(true);\n});\n\ntest(\"REVIEW: publication transport diagnostics contain only fixed codes\", async () => {\n  const f = await lifecycleFixture();\n  const privateText = [\"review\", \"private\", \"transport\"].join(\"-\");\n  writeFileSync(join(f.h.cfg.paths.configDir, \"private-strings.txt\"), privateText);\n  const q = f.store.askQuestion(f.run.id, privateText);\n  f.store.updateRun(f.run.id, { status: \"waiting_input\" });\n  f.h.intercept = (args) => {\n    if (args[1]?.endsWith(\"/comments\") && args.includes(\"POST\"))\n      throw new Error(`transport diagnostic ${privateText}`);\n  };\n  await f.poll();\n  expect(f.effect([q.id])?.body).toContain(\"[withheld; see the UI]\");\n  expect(f.h.logs.join(\"\\n\")).not.toContain(privateText);\n});\n\n\ntest.each([\"prepared\", \"identity saved\", \"issuing\", \"before ack\", \"after ack\"])(\n  \"REVIEW checkpoint: restart at %s publishes once\", async (cut) => {\n    const f = await lifecycleFixture();\n    const q = f.store.askQuestion(f.run.id, \"checkpoint question\");\n    f.store.updateRun(f.run.id, { status: \"waiting_input\" });\n    if (cut === \"prepared\") {\n      await f.poll(0);\n      f.reopen();\n      await f.poll();\n      f.reopen();\n      await f.poll();\n      expect(f.h.comments.get(7)).toHaveLength(1);\n      expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"done\", commentId: 7001 });\n      return;\n    }\n    const write = f.store.setIssueLifecycleEffect.bind(f.store);\n    let fired = false;\n    const spy = spyOn(f.store, \"setIssueLifecycleEffect\").mockImplementation((...args) => {\n      const [, , , effect, state, details] = args;\n      const matches = effect === `comment:questions:${q.id}` && (\n        (cut === \"prepared\" && state === \"pending\" && details?.body && !details.login) ||\n        (cut === \"identity saved\" && state === \"pending\" && details?.login && !details.page) ||\n        (cut === \"issuing\" && details?.page === 1) ||\n        ((cut === \"before ack\" || cut === \"after ack\") && state === \"done\" && details?.commentId)\n      );\n      if (matches && !fired) {\n        fired = true;\n        if (cut === \"before ack\") throw new Error(\"checkpoint interrupted\");\n        write(...args);\n        throw new Error(\"checkpoint interrupted\");\n      }\n      write(...args);\n    });\n    try { await f.poll().catch(() => {}); } finally { spy.mockRestore(); }\n    expect(fired).toBe(true);\n    f.reopen();\n    await f.poll();\n    f.reopen();\n    await f.poll();\n    expect(f.h.comments.get(7)).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"done\", commentId: 7001 });\n  },\n);\n\ntest(\"REVIEW coverage: terminal recovering run stays in work selection after restart\", async () => {\n  const f = await lifecycleFixture();\n  const q = f.store.askQuestion(f.run.id, \"question\");\n  f.store.updateRun(f.run.id, { status: \"waiting_input\" });\n  f.h.comments.set(7, Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, i) => `discussion ${i}`));\n  f.h.intercept = (args) => {\n    if (args[1]?.endsWith(\"/comments\") && args.includes(\"POST\")) throw new Error(\"not accepted\");\n  };\n  await f.poll();\n  f.h.intercept = undefined;\n  f.store.updateRun(f.run.id, { status: \"cancelled\" });\n  f.store.setIssueLifecycleEffect(f.run.id, \"owner/repo\", 7, \"labels\", \"none\");\n  f.store.setIssueLifecycleEffect(f.run.id, \"owner/repo\", 7, \"comment:cancelled\", \"done\");\n  await f.poll(1);\n  expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"recovering\", page: 2 });\n  f.reopen();\n  await f.poll();\n  expect(f.effect([q.id])).toMatchObject({ state: \"done\", commentId: null });\n  expect(f.h.comments.get(7)).toHaveLength(100);\n});\n```"
